<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S7.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16505v1/figures/devices_objectives_avg.png" id="S7.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S7.F6.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S7.F6.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Avg Devices Loss</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S7.F6.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16505v1/figures/server_objectives1.png" id="S7.F6.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S7.F6.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S7.F6.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Server Val Loss</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S7.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 6</span>: </span><span id="S7.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Objective Values</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S7.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Loss.</span>
With objective functions, we understand the loss value to examine how the optimizer performs and converges during the optimization process.
With a maximum value of 100 for the COBYLA optimizer, the convergence is studied with experimental analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The result for the average of all devices is shown in Figure <a href="#S7.F6.sf1" title="In Fig. 6 ‣ VII-B Results. ‣ VII Experiment ‣ orb-QFL: Orbital Quantum Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6(a)</span></a>.
Similarly, for the server, the objective values are better with orb-QFL, which is shown in Figure <a href="#S7.F6.sf2" title="In Fig. 6 ‣ VII-B Results. ‣ VII Experiment ‣ orb-QFL: Orbital Quantum Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6(b)</span></a>.
These results point towards better practicality and performance of the proposed approach.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Link Budget Analysis.</span>
Link Budget Analysis was performed using Matlab.
We consider two LEO satellites at an altitude of 500 km, which are separate by 72 degrees in terms of longitude. A geostationary satellite is considered with altitude of 20 m above earth surface almost in the equidistant from both satellites. For this experiment, we neglected the loss factors from all satellites and the geostationary satellite.
Thus, we compare the links between station to satellite (L1), satellite to station (L2) , and satellite to satellite (L3).
The properties of links (L1, L2) include a frequency of 2 GHz, a bandwidth of 6 MHz, a bitrate of 10 Mbps, and a required Eb/No of 10 dB. The transmitter on Satellite (S1) has a Tx HPA power of 17 dBW, a Tx HPA OBO of 6 dB, and a Tx antenna gain of 60 dBi. The receiver on Satellite (S2) has an Rx G/T of 10 dB/K. Additionally, the properties of Link (L3) include a frequency of 2.2 GHz, a bandwidth of 5 MHz, a bitrate of 10 Mbps and a required Eb/No of 10 dB.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">From the contour plot shown in Figures <a href="#S7.F7.sf1" title="In Fig. 7 ‣ VII-B Results. ‣ VII Experiment ‣ orb-QFL: Orbital Quantum Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(a)</span></a>, <a href="#S7.F7.sf2" title="In Fig. 7 ‣ VII-B Results. ‣ VII Experiment ‣ orb-QFL: Orbital Quantum Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(b)</span></a> and <a href="#S7.F7.sf3" title="In Fig. 7 ‣ VII-B Results. ‣ VII Experiment ‣ orb-QFL: Orbital Quantum Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(c)</span></a>, we compare the high amplifier power (HPA) versus distance (km).
With contour lines, we observe the margin value (dB), which is the excess SNR threshold value required for reliable communication.
From Figures <a href="#S7.F7.sf1" title="In Fig. 7 ‣ VII-B Results. ‣ VII Experiment ‣ orb-QFL: Orbital Quantum Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(a)</span></a>, <a href="#S7.F7.sf2" title="In Fig. 7 ‣ VII-B Results. ‣ VII Experiment ‣ orb-QFL: Orbital Quantum Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(b)</span></a> and <a href="#S7.F7.sf3" title="In Fig. 7 ‣ VII-B Results. ‣ VII Experiment ‣ orb-QFL: Orbital Quantum Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(c)</span></a>, G2S operates at around 44 dB and 14 dBW power, S2G at around 40 dB with 17 dbW power and the
S2S link at about 50 dB with 16 dbW power.
The inter-satellite communication clearly has a better margin, which indicates that communication to and from the Earth station or any server thereby needs more power and provides less margin which can cause unreliable communication in comparison to orb-QFL setting where most transfer and receiving happens only between satellites themselves.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S7.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S7.F7.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16505v1/figures/s2g_hpa_vs_dist1.png" id="S7.F7.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/418;" width="476" height="418" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S7.F7.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S7.F7.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">S2G</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S7.F7.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16505v1/figures/g2s_hpa_vs_dist1.png" id="S7.F7.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/415;" width="476" height="415" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S7.F7.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S7.F7.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">G2S</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S7.F7.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16505v1/figures/s2s_hpa_vs_dist1.png" id="S7.F7.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/407;" width="476" height="407" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S7.F7.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S7.F7.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">S2S</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S7.F7.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16505v1/figures/fspl_vs_distance1.png" id="S7.F7.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/461;" width="476" height="461" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S7.F7.sf4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(d)</span> </span><span id="S7.F7.sf4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">FSPL</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S7.F7.sf5" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16505v1/figures/margin_vs_bitrate1.png" id="S7.F7.sf5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/402;" width="476" height="402" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S7.F7.sf5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(e)</span> </span><span id="S7.F7.sf5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Bitrate</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S7.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 7</span>: </span><span id="S7.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Link Budged Analysis</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S7.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S7.F7.sf4" title="In Fig. 7 ‣ VII-B Results. ‣ VII Experiment ‣ orb-QFL: Orbital Quantum Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(d)</span></a> represents Free Space Path Loss (FSPL) versus distance for three different links L1, L2 and L3.
In this case, L1 is the best-performing link in terms of FSPL having the lowest path loss at a given distance which means it experiences the least signal degradation over distance.
Whereas, L2 suffers from the highest FSPL.
Thus, L3 comes in between two other link properties.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S7.F7.sf5" title="In Fig. 7 ‣ VII-B Results. ‣ VII Experiment ‣ orb-QFL: Orbital Quantum Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(e)</span></a> shows the margin (in dB) as a function of the bit rate (in Mbps) for the links.
All lines display a decrease in margin with an increase in bitrate which is as expected.
Amongst the links, L3 has the highest margin than the others indicating better reliability than the others.
Thus, orb-QFL which is dependent more on direct satellite-to-satellite communication provides further advantages along with improved performance of the QFL network.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Lastly, it is to be noted that the default QFL means that both L1 and L2 links are involved.
But in orb-QFL, there is only an L3 link available with only need for L1 and L2 link communication once a while only after the end of all the communication rounds.
Thus, these results show how robust and reliable orb-QFL can be validating the practicality of this work.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VIII </span><span id="S8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Conclusion</span></h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we first presented a novel approach to continuous QFL framework integration training without any server aggregation procedure involved.
Along with it, our study explores the applicability of QFL with our approach to LEO satellite network communications to improve communication efficiency and solve many bottleneck issues involved in SATCOM settings.
Through our theoretical and experimental investigation, we demonstrated both the practicality and feasibility of our method within satellite networks.
Our research will serve as an essential foundation for future studies in quantum federated learning (QFL) and satellite constellation communications, paving the way for advancements in next-generation machine learning and communication networks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IX </span><span id="S9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">APPENDIX</span></h2>

<section id="S9.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S9.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IX-A</span> </span><span id="S9.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Lemma 1.</span></h3>

<div id="S9.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S9.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz continuous with constant <math id="S9.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="S9.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S9.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|F(\theta)-F(\theta^{\prime})|\leq L\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|F(\theta)-F(\theta^{\prime})|\leq L\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">COBYLA optimizer constructs a trust region around the current point <math id="S9.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and solves a subproblem within this region</p>
<table id="S9.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{d}F(\theta_{t}+d)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>d</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{d}F(\theta_{t}+d)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">subject to
<math id="S9.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|d\|\leq\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|d\|\leq\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, <math id="S9.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the radius of the trust region.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In each iteration <math id="S9.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, COBYLA updates the point <math id="S9.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S9.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> by solving the sub-problem, ensuring that <math id="S9.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t}\|\leq\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t}\|\leq\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The regret <math id="S9.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{F}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{F}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> is the sum of differences between the function values at <math id="S9.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S9.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{F}(T)=\sum_{t=1}^{T}[F(\theta_{t})-F(\theta^{*})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{F}(T)=\sum_{t=1}^{T}[F(\theta_{t})-F(\theta^{*})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using the Lipschitz continuity of <math id="S9.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, we can bound the difference as,</p>
<table id="S9.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\theta_{t})-F(\theta^{*})\leq L\|\theta_{t}-\theta^{*}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\theta_{t})-F(\theta^{*})\leq L\|\theta_{t}-\theta^{*}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">By triangle inequality, we know</p>
<table id="S9.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta_{t}-\theta^{*}\|\leq\|\theta_{t}-\theta_{t-1}\|+\|\theta_{t-1}-\theta^{*}\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta_{t}-\theta^{*}\|\leq\|\theta_{t}-\theta_{t-1}\|+\|\theta_{t-1}-\theta^{*}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S9.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t}\|\leq\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t}\|\leq\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, by iterating the inequality, we can have,</p>
<table id="S9.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta_{t}-\theta^{*}\|\leq\sum_{k=1}^{t}\Delta_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta_{t}-\theta^{*}\|\leq\sum_{k=1}^{t}\Delta_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="S9.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\theta_{t})-F(\theta^{*})\leq L\|\theta_{t}-\theta^{*}\|\leq L\sum_{k=1}^{t}\Delta_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\theta_{t})-F(\theta^{*})\leq L\|\theta_{t}-\theta^{*}\|\leq L\sum_{k=1}^{t}\Delta_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Summing the bound on <math id="S9.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\theta_{t})-F(\theta^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\theta_{t})-F(\theta^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S9.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> from 1 to <math id="S9.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S9.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{F}(T)=\sum_{t=1}^{T}[F(\theta_{t})-F(\theta^{*})]\leq L\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Delta_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{F}(T)=\sum_{t=1}^{T}[F(\theta_{t})-F(\theta^{*})]\leq L\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Delta_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This proof confirms that the regret <math id="S9.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{F}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{F}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> of the COBYLA optimizer after <math id="S9.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> iterations is bounded by <math id="S9.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S9.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">IX-B</span> </span><span id="S9.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Theorem 1.</span></h3>

<div id="S9.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, we have upper bound for global model with learning rate <math id="S9.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, effective learning rate denoted by <math id="S9.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> with Stochastic Gradient Descent as,</p>
<table id="S9.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E\left[F(\theta^{R})-F(\theta^{*})\right]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E\left[F(\theta^{R})-F(\theta^{*})\right]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{9}{2}\mu D^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\tilde{\eta}R}{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{9}{2}\mu D^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\tilde{\eta}R}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{12\tilde{\eta}\sigma^{2}}{NK}+\frac{18L\tilde{\eta}^{2}\sigma^{2}}{NK}+\frac{18L\tilde{\eta}^{2}\zeta^{2}_{*}}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{12\tilde{\eta}\sigma^{2}}{NK}+\frac{18L\tilde{\eta}^{2}\sigma^{2}}{NK}+\frac{18L\tilde{\eta}^{2}\zeta^{2}_{*}}{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where, <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{R}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the weighted average of the global model parameters after <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> rounds. <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the global objective function and <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> signifies the optimal solution to this global objective function. The effective learning rate is denoted by <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="S9.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the initial distance between the starting point and the optimal solution. The variance of the stochastic gradient is represented by <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="S9.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta^{2}_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta^{2}_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant that measures the heterogeneity of local objective functions in the optimal solution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Considering the optimizer factor, we have,</p>
<table id="S9.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E\left[F(\theta^{R})-F(\theta^{*})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E\left[F(\theta^{R})-F(\theta^{*})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{9}{2}\mu D^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\tilde{\eta}R}{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{9}{2}\mu D^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\tilde{\eta}R}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{12\tilde{\eta}\sigma^{2}}{NK}+\frac{18L\tilde{\eta}^{2}\sigma^{2}}{NK}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{12\tilde{\eta}\sigma^{2}}{NK}+\frac{18L\tilde{\eta}^{2}\sigma^{2}}{NK}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{18L\tilde{\eta}^{2}\zeta^{2}_{*}}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{18L\tilde{\eta}^{2}\zeta^{2}_{*}}{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Then,</p>
<table id="S9.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E\left[F(\theta^{R})-F(\theta^{*})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E\left[F(\theta^{R})-F(\theta^{*})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{L}{R}\sum_{t=1}^{R}\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{L}{R}\sum_{t=1}^{R}\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{9}{2}\mu D^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\tilde{\eta}R}{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{9}{2}\mu D^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\tilde{\eta}R}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{12\tilde{\eta}\sigma^{2}}{NK}+\frac{18L\tilde{\eta}^{2}\sigma^{2}}{NK}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{12\tilde{\eta}\sigma^{2}}{NK}+\frac{18L\tilde{\eta}^{2}\sigma^{2}}{NK}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{18L\tilde{\eta}^{2}\zeta^{2}_{*}}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{18L\tilde{\eta}^{2}\zeta^{2}_{*}}{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Replacing <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and relaxing heterogeneity aspect,</p>
<table id="S9.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{L}{R}\sum_{t=1}^{R}\Delta_{t}+\frac{9}{2}\mu D^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\Delta_{t}R}{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{L}{R}\sum_{t=1}^{R}\Delta_{t}+\frac{9}{2}\mu D^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\Delta_{t}R}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{12\Delta_{t}\sigma^{2}}{NK}+\frac{18L\Delta_{t}^{2}\sigma^{2}}{NK}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{12\Delta_{t}\sigma^{2}}{NK}+\frac{18L\Delta_{t}^{2}\sigma^{2}}{NK}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now considering, Sat-Comm and Quantum computational factors,</p>
<table id="S9.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{L}{R}\sum_{t=1}^{R}\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{L}{R}\sum_{t=1}^{R}\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{9}{2}\mu D^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\Delta_{t}R}{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{9}{2}\mu D^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\Delta_{t}R}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{12\Delta_{t}\sigma^{2}}{NK}+\frac{18L\Delta_{t}^{2}\sigma^{2}}{NK}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{12\Delta_{t}\sigma^{2}}{NK}+\frac{18L\Delta_{t}^{2}\sigma^{2}}{NK}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\Delta_{C}+\Delta_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\Delta_{C}+\Delta_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where,
<math id="S9.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{C}=\gamma_{c}\tau_{c}R+\delta_{c}\rho_{loss}\rho+\epsilon_{c}\frac{\rho}{B}T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{C}=\gamma_{c}\tau_{c}R+\delta_{c}\rho_{loss}\rho+\epsilon_{c}\frac{\rho}{B}T</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="S9.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{Q}=\alpha_{q}\sigma_{q}^{2}N_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{Q}=\alpha_{q}\sigma_{q}^{2}N_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, with further simplification,</p>
<table id="S9.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E[F(\bar{x}_{R})-F(x^{*})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E[F(\bar{x}_{R})-F(x^{*})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{L}{R}\sum_{t=1}^{R}\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{L}{R}\sum_{t=1}^{R}\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mu D^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\Delta_{t}R}{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mu D^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\Delta_{t}R}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{\Delta_{t}}{NK}+\frac{L\Delta_{t}^{2}}{NK}+\Delta_{C}+\Delta_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{\Delta_{t}}{NK}+\frac{L\Delta_{t}^{2}}{NK}+\Delta_{C}+\Delta_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Then,</p>
<table id="S9.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E\left[F(\theta^{R})-F(\theta^{*})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E\left[F(\theta^{R})-F(\theta^{*})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\underbrace{L\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Delta_{t}}_{\text{Optimizer}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Optimizer</mtext></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\underbrace{L\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Delta_{t}}_{\text{Optimizer}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{\mu(\theta_{0}-\theta^{*})^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\Delta_{t}R}{2}\right)}_{\text{FL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>FL</mtext></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{\mu(\theta_{0}-\theta^{*})^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu\Delta_{t}R}{2}\right)}_{\text{FL}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
